label day1_food_route:
    scene bg park
    show plato at center_slot
    with dissolve

    pl "Hey, what's up!? It's so good to see you! Guess what, I have so much to tell you!"

    r "Hi! This is exciting, what did you learn?"

    pl "Ok, so you know how recycling has improved a lot over the last few years? Advancements in recycling technology have allowed for this! This includes things like the usage of biological recycling, where enzymes or microenzymes are used to break down biodegradable or compostable plastics."

    r "Wait, really? I didn't know things were so advanced."

    pl "Yeah, it's awesome! Biodegradable plastics can be broken down naturally through micro-organisms - including bacteria, fungi, and invertebrates, while compostable plastic can only biodegrade under specific conditions to produce compost. There's also anaerobic digestion, where specific microorganisms can decompose plastic in the absence of oxygen. This method is gaining traction because the byproducts (methane and carbon dioxide) can be used as energy, and using micro-organisms in general saves a lot of energy and resources. Isn't that so, super cool!?"

    r "That's super interesting... Y'know, thanks to this sort of research, recycling has really advanced a lot, huh?"

    pl "It sure has!"

    return
